15. (Currently Amended) A method of selecting a server computer for sending data to a client computer, the method comprising the steps of:
accessing a server computer through a path in a computer network, the path including one or more server computers;
adding information indicative of at least one server computer of the first set of one or more server computers to a locator of a resource on the second server computer, the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier, wherein the information is added __prior to transmission of the locator to the client computer__;
selecting the first server computer based on the information added to the locator, __wherein the selection occurs at a media request broker that receives the locator from the client computer and determines the first server computer based on real-time server load or availability metrics contained in the information__.

16. (Currently Amended) The method of claim 15, __wherein the second server computer is a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature that is dynamically generated based on server selection criteria, the method further comprising the steps of selecting the hyperlink by the client computer, and subsequently generating an http request out of this hyperlink by a web browser, this http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request, wherein the media request broker receives the http request and selects the first server computer based on the unique signature and current server performance data__.

